# GovScheme Project Context

Updated: 2026-11-17

This file is a handoff for future work on the repository. It summarizes the project, its current behavior, recent decisions, and the user-request history available in this conversation. It is not a verbatim export of every assistant message or tool result.

## Project overview

GovScheme is a web application for discovering Indian government schemes. The repository has a React/Vite frontend and a Node.js/Express backend backed by MySQL. The frontend provides scheme search and browsing, scheme details, an admin login and scheme-creation prototype, and a browser-local saved-schemes list.

## Repository layout

- `React/` — React 18, TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind, React Router, and UI components.
- `React/src/pages/` — Homepage, dashboard, scheme directory and details, category/ministries/locations views, login/profile, and informational pages.
- `React/src/components/` — Shared navigation, saved-scheme UI, and reusable UI components.
- `React/src/lib/` — API client, translations, utilities, and saved-scheme local storage provider.
- `Backend/` — Node.js 20+ and Express 5 API.
- `Backend/src/routes/` — API routes for auth, schemes, categories, ministries, locations, genders, and criteria options.
- `Backend/migrations/` — Ordered MySQL schema and master-data migrations.
- `Backend/scripts/seed-admin.js` — Admin bootstrap and idempotent seeding for detailed Education schemes and the general scheme catalog.
- `Backend/scripts/scheme-catalog.js` — Broad catalog seed data.
- `Backend/tests/` — Node's built-in test runner tests.

The React package is currently named `UXPilot` in its `package.json`; the UI itself identifies as GovScheme. There is no root-level README. `Backend/README.md` documents backend setup and API behavior, but its Education scheme count predates the latest seed addition; use the seeder and tests as the current source for that count.

## Current frontend behavior

- `/` is a welcome homepage for the scheme portal.
- `/dashboard` contains the centered scheme search and featured schemes.
- `/schemes` lists schemes; `/schemes/:id` shows scheme details.
- `/saved-schemes` is a separate navigation section between Ministries and States & UTs. Save actions in scheme listings and details add scheme IDs to browser local storage.
- Statistics and the chart page/sections were removed at the user's request.
- The homepage category-browsing section was removed.
- `/how-it-works` and `/help` are the informational pages.

Relevant files include `React/src/App.tsx`, `React/src/pages/Index.tsx`, `React/src/pages/Dashboard.tsx`, `React/src/components/PortalHeader.tsx`, `React/src/components/SavedSchemesSection.tsx`, and `React/src/lib/savedSchemes.tsx`.

## Backend and data notes

- Backend setup requires Node.js 20+, MySQL, and environment values copied from `Backend/.env.example`. Never copy actual `.env` values into documentation or source control.
- Run backend commands from `Backend/`: `npm install`, `npm run db:migrate`, `npm run db:seed-admin`, `npm run dev`, and `npm test`.
- Migrations are applied by `Backend/scripts/migrate.js` and tracked in `schema_migrations`.
- Scheme details, benefits, eligibility, application process, and documents are stored as JSON; scheme category mappings are relational.
- The `db:seed-admin` command writes to the configured database. It seeds the admin, detailed Education scheme records, and the full catalog. Do not run it against an unknown or live database without confirming the target.
- The detailed Education seeder currently includes PM-USP-CSSS, NMMSS, AICTE Pragati, AICTE Saksham, and PM-Vidyalaxmi. The broader catalog also tags PM-YASASVI and INSPIRE under Education; together these make seven Education schemes in the seeded data.
- PM-Vidyalaxmi uses the official portal `https://pmvidyalaxmi.co.in/` as a reference. Its loan terms, lender assessment, institute eligibility, and any interest support must be checked against current official rules; do not imply that applications are always open or promise a fixed amount.
- Scheme eligibility, benefit values, application dates, and availability can change. Direct users to the administering agency's current guidelines.
- Scheme creation is currently public in the backend prototype; the Backend README notes it must be protected by admin authorization before production.

